{title: For Such a Time as This}
{subtitle: Esther 4:10–17}
{key: D}
{tempo: 87}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D] | [A/C#] | [Bm] [F#m/A] | [G] [D/F#] |
| [Em7] [A7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Everyone [A/C#]knows, the [Bm]law of [G]the king
Whoev[D/F#]er goes in to him [D]uncalled shall die
Un[A/C#]less he [Bm]holds [Dmaj7/A]out the gold[G]en scepter
And [D/F#]I have [Em7]not been [G]called these thirty days
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A7/G]Do not think [D/F#]that [G]in the king's palace
[A7]You will es[D]cape more than [G]all the Jews
For if [A7/G]you keep si[D/F#]lent at this time
Relief will rise from another place
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[A/C#]And who knows [Dmaj7/A]whether [G]you have come
[D/F#]To the kin[Em7]gdom for [A7]such a [D]time as [A/C#]this
Who [Dmaj7/A]knows, who knows
For such a [G]time as this
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Go, gather [A7/G]all the Jews [D/F#]in Susa
Fast for me, three days, [G]night or day
Then I will go [A7/G]to the king, though it [D/F#]is against the law
[A/C#]And if I [Dmaj7/A]perish, [G]I perish
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D/F#]And who knows [Em7]whether [A7]you have [D]come
To [A/C#]the kin[Dmaj7/A]gdom for such a time as this
Who knows, who knows
For such a time as [D]this
{end_of_chorus}

